    LLM: 'Game: Italian Poker. Objective: Primary objective: Meet the game winning condition.',
    Player: 'Italian Poker: play by the rules, manage scoring opportunities, and pursue the win condition.',
    objective: 'Win the pot by having the highest-ranking hand at showdown, or by being the last player standing when all others have folded.',
    gameplay: 'Ante; optional blind (buio, controbuio, over) before deal. Deal 5 cards each. First betting round: pass or open (with pair of Jacks or better, or 4-card straight-flush draw); then fold, call, raise. Draw: each surviving player may exchange 0–4 cards. Second betting round: bet, check, or parol (throw in and carry pot); then fold, call, raise. Showdown: highest hand wins; flush beats full house; straight flush has min/medium/max with min beating max.',
    keyRules: [
      'Opening requires pair of Jacks or better, or four consecutive cards of a suit (no Ace) that can extend to straight flush.',
      'Flush ranks above full house. Straight flush: minimum beats maximum, maximum beats medium, medium beats minimum.',
      'Ties broken by suit order: hearts highest, then diamonds, clubs, spades.',
      'Direction of play is clockwise.',
